2.—(1) In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“approved gaming equipment” means gaming equipment of a class approved by the Authority under regulation 21(7) for use in a casino;
[S 64/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
[Deleted by S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“approved manufacturer” means a manufacturer of gaming machines or gaming programs that is approved by the Authority under regulation 5(1) as an approved manufacturer;
[S 64/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
[Deleted by S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“approved test service provider” means a provider of testing services that is approved by the Authority under regulation 24B(1) as an approved test service provider;
[S 64/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“authorised supplier”, in relation to an approved manufacturer, means a person that the approved manufacturer has notified the Authority under section 103A(4)(c) of the Act is a supplier that will be used to supply gaming machines or gaming programs of the approved manufacturer;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“business associate”, in relation to an approved manufacturer, an approved test service provider or an applicant to be an approved manufacturer or approved test service provider, means any person, body or association who, in the opinion of the Authority, has a business association with (but is not an associate within the meaning in paragraph (2) of) the approved manufacturer, approved test service provider or applicant, as the case may be;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“manager”, in relation to a manufacturing facility, means any person who administers or manages the manufacturing facility, but does not include an approved manufacturer or an applicant to be an approved manufacturer;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“manufacturing facility”, in relation to an approved manufacturer or an applicant to be an approved manufacturer, means any premises or facility —
(a)used or intended to be used (as the case may be) by the approved manufacturer or applicant (whether by itself or through another person) to manufacture any gaming machine or gaming program of the approved manufacturer or applicant for use in any casino; and
(b)at which the finished product of the gaming machine or gaming program is manufactured or assembled;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
[Deleted by S 64/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
“modification”, in relation to any approved gaming machine, approved gaming program, approved gaming equipment or approved linked jackpot arrangement, means any change —
(a)affecting the display or operation of the approved gaming machine, approved gaming program, approved gaming equipment or approved linked jackpot arrangement; or
(b)capable of affecting the outcome of the casino gambling carried out on that approved gaming machine, with that approved gaming equipment or using that approved gaming program or approved linked jackpot arrangement;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“official website” means the website of the Authority at https://www.gra.gov.sg;
[S 64/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
[S 643/2022 wef 01/08/2022]
“relevant financial interest”, in relation to a business, means —
(a)any share in the capital of the business;
(b)any entitlement to receive any income derived from the business; or
(c)any contribution to the capital of the business, whether by a loan or otherwise;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“relevant position”, in relation to a business, means the position of director or manager, or other executive position, however that position is designated;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“relevant power” means any power, whether exercisable by voting or otherwise and whether exercisable alone or in association with others —
(a)to participate in any directorial, managerial or executive decision; or
(b)to elect or appoint any person to any relevant position;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
[Deleted by S 64/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
“return to player percentage” or “RTP%” means the theoretical return to a player of the value of all prizes awarded by a casino game (including any external prize) as a percentage of all bets made on that game over a large volume of game play;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“supplier”, in relation to an approved manufacturer or an applicant to be an approved manufacturer, means any person that the approved manufacturer or applicant uses or intends to use (as the case may be) to supply its gaming machines or gaming programs;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
[Deleted by S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“technical standards”, in relation to any gaming machine, gaming program or other gaming equipment of a particular class or description, means the technical standards issued or approved by the Authority under section 200B(1) of the Act applicable to gaming machines, gaming programs or gaming equipment of that class or description, updated from time to time and made available to the casino operators and any other person required to comply with them.
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(2) In these Regulations, a person is an “associate” of an approved manufacturer, an approved test service provider or an applicant to be an approved manufacturer or approved test service provider if the person is or will be, in the opinion of the Authority, able to exercise a significant influence over or with respect to the management or operation of the business of the approved manufacturer, approved test service provider or applicant.
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(3) In determining whether a person is able or will be able to exercise the significant influence referred to in paragraph (2), the Authority may consider all or any of the following:
(a)whether the person holds or will hold any relevant financial interest in the business of the approved manufacturer, approved test service provider or applicant;
(b)whether the person is or will be entitled to exercise any relevant power (whether in right of the person or on behalf of any other person) in the business of the approved manufacturer, approved test service provider or applicant;
(c)whether the person holds or will hold any relevant position (whether in right of the person or on behalf of any other person) in the business of the approved manufacturer, approved test service provider or applicant;
(d)the degree of direct or indirect influence that the person has in the management or operation of the business of the approved manufacturer, approved test service provider or applicant;
(e)any other matter that the Authority considers relevant.
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]

24D.—(1) Every approved test service provider shall comply with all of the following duties:
(a)notify the Authority in writing of the happening of any of the matters set out in the Third Schedule, as soon as practicable and, in any event, no later than 14 days after becoming aware that the event has occurred or such longer period as the Authority may allow in any particular case;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(b)when requested by the Authority to do so —
(i)provide to the Authority such information as the Authority may specify;
(ii)produce such records as the Authority may specify and permit the Authority to examine the records, take extracts from them and make copies of them; and
(iii)furnish such authorisation or consent as the Authority may direct for the purpose of enabling the Authority to obtain information (including financial and other confidential information) concerning the approved test service provider and any associate of the approved test service provider from other persons;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(c)attend before the Authority or an inspector in relation to any matters relevant to its approval as an approved test service provider, or to other matters specified by the Authority, and to answer questions relating to those matters.
(2) Every approved test service provider shall, in addition, comply with all of the following requirements:
(a)maintain its accreditation by such professional accreditation organisation as the Authority may specify by a notice in writing to be published on the official website of the Authority;
(b)provide such written undertakings as may be required by the Authority in furtherance of the objectives of these Regulations;
(c)ensure that it meets any code, standard of performance, specification or requirement given by the Authority in relation to the testing services provided by it under these Regulations;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(d)attend periodic meetings with the Authority when requested to do so;
(e)where the approved test service provider has no place of business in Singapore, notify the Authority of an address in Singapore for the service of any document to be served in proceedings in court and a person or persons authorised to accept service on its behalf;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(f)ensure that it does not assign, delegate, sub-contract or engage any person not directly employed by the approved test service provider to carry out the testing of gaming equipment without the prior written approval of the Authority;
(g)allow the Authority, its officers or agents to inspect any premises in Singapore or elsewhere where the approved test service provider carries on business, (including but not limited to the test facilities of the approved test service provider) for the purposes of an investigation under regulation 24H;
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(h)when requested to do so by written notice given by the Authority, provide to the Authority, within the period specified in the notice, such information or document in such form and manner requested which —
(i)relates to any matter in the Fourth Schedule as it applies to any person mentioned in regulation 24H(1); and
(ii)is relevant to be considered by the Authority for the purposes of a determination mentioned in regulation 24H(1) of the approved test service provider’s suitability to continue as an approved test service provider.
[S 641/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(3) The Authority, its officers or its agents shall not be liable to pay any person any fee, charge or expense on account of any inspection under paragraph (2)(g).
(4) If any approved test service provider fails to comply with any of the requirements under this regulation, the Authority may, by notice in writing, require the approved test service provider to rectify the failure or take such other corrective action within a specified time as the Authority may determine.
[S 64/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
